-STATEMENT CALL DYNAMIC_CONNECTIVITY_QUERY('Person', 0, 5, 'dc_dtree_csr') RETURN *;
---- 1
False

# Parallel relationships are deliberately not covered yet.
#
# Two relationships over the same ordered pair need multiplicity-aware
# maintenance: deleting one must leave the endpoints connected while the other
# survives. The CSR-backed backends are expected to get this right for free
# once the path is settled, because the provider re-reads the base CSR and the
# surviving edge is returned as the replacement. stree/dtree cannot: their
# insertEdge returns early when the endpoints are already tree-linked, so the
# second edge is dropped rather than recorded as a non-tree edge.
#
# Add a DCNeighbourProviderParallelRelationships case once the implementation
# is ready. Until then these tests keep one relationship per ordered pair, so
# every expected value above is independent of multiplicity handling.
